Z||000010||stimpy||11-03-2001||07:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kempo:<BR><B><BR>For $4000 worth for swapping motors into a $1000 fiero, total of $5000, could tear up a cobra and gt, which is under half the cost of one.  This is an unmodifyed motor.  Spend another $1500 on it, as you'd put it, minimal mods, the fiero would be running 12's flat in the quarter, still tearing up the mustangs, again, under half the cost.[b]<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Uh, do you have one of these magical $5000 Fieros that will clean up Mustang Cobras? Have you even done a swap? I mean, I love Fieros and all, but that is complete and total boolsheet. First off, a $1000 Fiero is gonna need more help then just the engine. You are not gonna find one with fresh brakes, steering and suspension for a grand. And if you do, chances are it will look like a$$.  Secondly, I find it very difficult to believe that anyone will contract to do a swap for $4000. MAYBE if you are talented enough and have the resources that Archie has, then you can bring a basic swap in at that. I mean, you are talking at least a SC3800 to have that kind of unbridaled scoot, and no-ones giving those away.<P>Face it, if you could get a reliable 13 second Fiero for $5000, we'd all have one. I know I would...<BR>||||reg||5
