Z||000012||Spektrum-87GT||11-03-2001||08:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>I seen a lot of people with v-8 fieros on here running 13's...thats what cobras and gts run with minimal mods (not massive engine swaps).  It will be closer than you think.<P>"You know something when the mustang or cav can do what BanditBalz can do, lift the front end almost ALL the way offthe ground STOCK, then I will be impressed."<P>engines in the front? like a normal car?  Duh?  Weirdo.<P><BR>And a 95 Z24 could beat a fiero gt if it was driven well.  They're fairly nice cars.<P>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 11-03-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>be a little more specific on what kind of v8 you're talking about... a 4.9 caddy with an automatic racing a new gt should be close... a hopped up sbc? wouldnt be. a 95 z24 and a fiero gt would be a very close race according to a few sites... they put the dohc 2.3l in that year, made 150hp, so it could go either way.<P>kempo: i noticed you have 0-60 in 6.9 in your signature... what kinda mods did you do? i'm looking for a time around there, just to hold me over until i get a v8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
