Z||000016||BlackStang95||11-04-2001||03:15 AM||||Spek he specified 4.9 caddy in the first post, thats what i was responding to, a hopped up sbc is far from a normal motor in any respect.<P>This is a fiero forum...you guys should take modified versions of fieros over stock versions of mustangs, no reason to post about it.  <P>That one dudes post has too many inaccuracies for me to really even respond to.  Of course taking an old fiero and modding it will cost you less than a new mustang gt from a dealership.  From a dealership loaded fieros costed a lot, nearly 17k, which adjusted for inflation, is a lot of money.  You should compare prices evenly, or not at all.  I'm glad some of your own took it to you.  <P>1996   Chevrolet Cavalier LS                  8.3            16.1<P>1988   Pontiac Fiero GT                       8.7            16.4<P><BR>That's from a site i found, it just lists a bunch of times, they seem to run on the slow side for all of em, but damn, that should put things in perspective.  <P>btw thats the ls, not even the z24, i know my stuff.<p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 11-04-2001).]||||reg||1
