Z||000032||grgoyl86||11-05-2001||02:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>first fiero, your comment didnt make any sense at all.   Any car can lurch the front end up (especially with bad shocks, lol) it's of course easier to do on a fiero because there is less weight in the front.  What part of that is not getting through to you?  Durrr<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>One other point on this "lifting the front end" thing. Look at the rotation of the Fiero engine. The torque will help in the effort. Now look at a Mustang. The motor is rotating perpendicular to the axle. Now, of course, some of the torque will try to make the differential gears lift the fron a little, but not a lot.<P>Nothing against either car, just a little bit of physics.<P>||||reg||6
