Z||000055||sdely||11-06-2001||11:46 AM||||Well, since the engine isn't the original one from the car the $1000 doesn't apply to the engine.  Actually my car would be perfect for a turbo since the ENGINE has under 70K miles on it, and was recently rebuilt.  Also it has a slightly lower compression ratio than stock.  Your idle conjecture is annoying, and if I choose to spend that money on the turbo I will do so.  I realize what I am saying is somewhat speculative, but don't treat me like my investment isn't worth anything.  You may think my investments are stupid but to me they make sense.  So use a $2000 Fiero, I don't care.  You'd still save money over the Stang.  I have researched it and it seems like a good idea to me.  So, who would put a turbo into a $1000 car?  Me, do you have a problem with that?  Does that make me stupid?  Cause if it does I'd really like to know.  I'd really like to know how you got to be so wise that you know exactley the condition of my vehicle and the appropriateness of a turbo application.<BR>$1000 dollar car to start with, then a new engine, then a turbo, what part of this do you not understand?<P>Seth<P>p.s. I already have a 200 horse car for under $3000, so thats where I get this stuff.  Sorry but my posts come from reality.  Plus the quote stimpy took was out of context, leaving out that it had a different engine.  I was talking of a specific car, and he ignorantly portrayed it as the rule about $1000 Fieros.  I propose a rule that I be treated like an intelligent human rather than an uninformed idiot.  Saying sarcastic comments such as "Where do you people get this stuff?", will only hurt your credibility, and miss quoting people (i.e. taking words out of context) won't help it much either.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by sdely (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000056||Borgio||11-06-2001||12:23 PM||||<BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Price: You can have LT1 ChopTop for the $20K. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>News to the owner, I'm sure. Hey Archie, will you build me a replica of the chop top for $20,000?<P>What's your deal? I was only meaning that is what it originally went for. Check Archie's site. Geez!<P>------------------<BR>Jake||||reg||1
